#!/bin/bash
cat <<'TXT'
COPYCAT — everything here is real Linux. These helpers only point you around.

  copycat-labs     list the labs (exercises live in ~/labs/NN-name/README.md)
  copycat-done NN  mark a lab finished (shows as [x] in copycat-labs)
  copycat-setup NN, copycat-check NN   graded labs: break it, fix it, get a score
  copycat-trouble  troubleshooting mode (copycat-trouble list)
  copysay [text]   a cat gives you a tip (or says what you type)
  copycat          reprint the banner

Machines
  copycat-kali     you are here        (user: copycat, password: copycat, sudo works)
  copycat-target   ssh student@copycat-target   (password: student)  http://copycat-target

Other users on this box: alex, sam, jordan (password: password)
Break something? Run copycat-reset in a terminal on your PC (not in here).
Leaving? copycat-stop on your PC keeps your changes; copycat-reset wipes them.
Prompt: =^.^= green means the last command worked, =^x^= red means it failed.
TXT
